test_dz_nin.doctest - detailed doctests for stdnum.dz.nin

Copyright (C) 2026

This file contains detailed tests for the structural validation of
Algerian NIN numbers.

>>> from stdnum.dz import nin

Valid structural examples. These examples test formatting and length,
not the issuance or authenticity of real identity numbers.

>>> nin.validate('123456789012345678')
'123456789012345678'
>>> nin.validate('123 456 789 012 345 678')
'123456789012345678'
>>> nin.validate('000000000000000000')
'000000000000000000'

Invalid length.

>>> nin.validate('12345678901234567')
Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
InvalidLength: ...
>>> nin.validate('1234567890123456789')
Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
InvalidLength: ...

Invalid characters.

>>> nin.validate('X23456789012345678')
Traceback (most recent call last):
    ...
InvalidFormat: ...

Validity checks.

>>> nin.is_valid('123456789012345678')
True
>>> nin.is_valid('123')
False
>>> nin.is_valid('X23456789012345678')
False

Formatting.

>>> nin.format('123 456 789 012 345 678')
'123456789012345678'
